UPDATE questions SET explanation = '<div class="explanation-rich-content"><div class="expl-card concept-card"><div class="section-title-concept">📌 Core Concept: IPv6 Multicast Scope</div><p>The 4th hex character of a multicast address tells you its scope. The scope limits how far the packet travels.</p><ul><li>FF02 = link-local. FF05 = site-local.</li><li>FF08 = organization-local. It is wider than site-local, for example all subnets in the company.</li><li>FF0E = global. It can be routed over the public Internet.</li></ul></div><div class="expl-card correct-card"><h4 class="section-title-correct">✓ Why the Correct Answer (Option D) is Correct:</h4><ul><li><span class="opt-tag correct">Option D</span> <strong>Organization-local</strong>: FF08 means organization-local scope.</li></ul></div><div class="expl-card incorrect-card"><h4 class="section-title-incorrect">✗ Why Other Options are Incorrect:</h4><ul><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option A</span> <strong>Global</strong>: That is the FF0E scope, not FF08.</li><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option B</span> <strong>Site-local</strong>: That is the FF05 scope, not FF08.</li><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option C</span> <strong>Link-local</strong>: That is the FF02 scope, not FF08.</li></ul></div><div class="expl-card tip-card"><h4 class="section-title-tip">💡 CCNA Exam Tip:</h4><p>Read the scope from the 4th hex character:</p><ul><li>1 interface.</li><li>2 link.</li><li>5 site.</li><li>8 organization.</li><li>E global.</li></ul></div><div class="expl-card concept-card"><div class="section-title-concept">📌 Source: Anki Flashcards - Network Fundamentals (CCNA / Day 32 Flashcards - IPv6 (Part 2)</div></div></div>' WHERE question_no = 'Anki-NF-1419';
